The inputs for the Black-Scholes equation are volatility, the price of the underlying asset, the strike price of the option, the time until the expiration of the option, the risk-free interest rate, and the type of option. It's theoretically possible for options sellers to set rational prices with these variables for the options they're selling. is NOT relevant, dump it.
